 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "In Malawi, school-leavers apply to the public universities through the National Council for Higher Education (NCHE), which advertises one public university selection each year after the MSCE results. Most degree programmes ask for at least six credits (grades 1 to 6) at MSCE including English, with good grades in the subjects that matter for the programme; competitive programmes such as medicine, engineering and law need mainly distinctions. Fees can be covered by the Higher Education Students' Loans and Grants Board, and private universities admit students directly.",
  "official_url": "https://www.nche.ac.mw",
  "notes": "UNIMA programme names are from the NCHE institution register, Mzuzu University names from its undergraduate programmes page and LUANAR names from the NCHE register. Mzuzu University and LUANAR do not publish faculty groupings on those pages, so the grouping here is Ace's own. Requirements change every year, so check the current NCHE call and each university before applying. UNIMA also offers a Bachelor of Laws (Honours), applied for through its own law admissions portal."
 },
